> The alternative is to change the API to not consume the data, but as it's an API change, I suggest we only add the warning.

The API isn't really changing if we just add `net_buf_simple_save(&buf->b, &state);` and `net_buf_simple_restore(&buf->b, &state);` at the beginning or end of the function IMO, but it will change the behavior slightly. 

Given that the current documentation does not state whether or not `bt_data_parse` modifies `ad`, I think we could get away with "fixing" it, rather than just adding the warning. 

We do have a few places in the stack where we actually assume that `bt_data_parse` consumes the data: 
```c
	/* Parse LTV entries */
	bt_data_parse(&ad, ascs_codec_config_store, codec);

	/* Check if all entries could be parsed */
	if (ad.len) {
```

but those are easily fixed I believe. 

The question is: Do we want `bt_data_parse` to consume the data or to be stateless?
